    "message": "Restate step-scoped TLA+ properties and fix unrunnable models\n\nTLC aborted at the first failing model, so only CanonicalBytes had been\nchecked since 2026-07-02. AuthorityFive did not parse, because the standard\nSequences module takes only a LOCAL INSTANCE of Naturals and so does not\nre-export Nat or the arithmetic operators. OrgPlanSync did not load, because\na .cfg cannot assign a record literal to a CONSTANT. Both run for the first\ntime now.\n\nThree guarantees were written as state invariants but describe a single\nstep, so an unrelated later action retroactively violated them:\n\n- F-G1 was broken by a warn-mode advisory merge followed by ToggleMode.\n- F-A1 and F-A5 were broken by revoking a grant after an authorized action.\n- F-D2 was broken by tampering after the PQC overlay was attached.\n\nThese are now temporal action properties declared with PROPERTY. Each was\nchecked against a negative control: an injected enforce-mode merge bypass,\nthe model's own EscalatePurchaseFromSearch, and DriftBug are all still\ncaught.\n\nWhere a model cached a verification result, the actions that mutate the\ninputs to that result now invalidate it. This matches 1922ab1 in\nCanonicalBytes and the implementation, which recomputes every gate decision\nfrom current repo state and per-call policy rather than caching one.\n\nF-G3 additionally gains an explicit evaluated flag, because envelope\nvalidity cannot imply a gate result that was never computed.\n\nF-O2 was the literal TRUE and F-A4 was absent entirely; both are now stated\nand checked. AuthorityFive bounds its append-only actionLog with a state\nconstraint so the model is finite. The PlusCal header comments no longer\nclaim to be the source of the hand-maintained modules.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n",
